{
  "title": "What Is a Function? — Reusable Recipes",
  "subtitle": "Packaging Logic with def and return",
  "topic": "6.1 • WHAT IS A FUNCTION?",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      6.1 • Modular Functions\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      What Is a <hlt>Function</hlt>?\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      A function is a named, reusable block of code that takes inputs (parameters), performs calculations, and produces an output (return value).\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      1. Real-World Analogy: Kitchen Blender\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Inputs In, Result Out\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      Think of a function like a kitchen blender:\n      <br/>• <strong>Parameters (Inputs):</strong> You drop in milk, bananas, and strawberries.\n      <br/>• <strong>Body (Processing):</strong> The blender blades run internal math/logic.\n      <br/>• <strong>Return Value (Output):</strong> It pours out a smoothie that you can assign to a glass variable!\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">def</span> <span style=\"color: #d2a8ff;\">make_smoothie</span>(fruit, liquid):<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;result = fruit + <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\" \"</span> + liquid + <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\" Smoothie\"</span><br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">return</span> result<br/><br/>\n      drink = make_smoothie(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Mango\"</span>, <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Milk\"</span>)<br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(drink)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: Mango Milk Smoothie</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #93c5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      2. Return vs Print\n    </span>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      • <code>print()</code> only displays text on the screen for human eyes. Other code cannot use the printed text.<br/>\n      • <code>return</code> sends data back into your code so it can be saved in a variable, passed to other functions, or used in math formulas!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}